eld need not be exported.\0A * \5Cparam E        The MPI to hold the public exponent.\0A *                 This may be \5Cc NULL if this field need not be exported.\0A *\0A * \5Creturn         \5Cc 0 on success.\0A * \5Creturn         #MBEDTLS_ERR_PLATFORM_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED if exporting the\0A *                 requested parameters cannot be done due to missing\0A *                 functionality or because of security policies.\0A * \5Creturn         A non-zero return code on any other failure.\0A *\0A */\0Aint mbedtls_rsa_export(const mbedtls_rsa_context *ctx,\0A                       mbedtls_mpi *N, mbedtls_mpi *P, mbedtls_mpi *Q,\0A                       mbedtls_mpi *D, mbedtls_mpi *E);\0A\0A/**\0A * \5Cbrief          This function exports core parameters of an RSA key\0A *                 in raw big-endian binary format.\0A *\0A *                 If this function runs successfully, the non-NULL buffers\0A *                 pointed to by \5Cp N, \5Cp P, \5Cp Q, \5Cp D, and \5Cp E are fully\0A *                 written, with additional unused space filled leading by\0A *                 zero Bytes.\0A *\0A *                 Possible reasons for returning\0A *                 #MBEDTLS_ERR_PLATFORM_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED:<ul>\0A *                 <li>An alternative RSA implementation is in use, which\0A *                 stores the key externally, and either cannot or should\0A *                 not export it into RAM.</li>\0A *                 <li>A SW or HW implementation might not support a certain\0A *                 deduction. For example, \5Cp P, \5Cp Q from \5Cp N, \5Cp D,\0A *                 and \5Cp E if the former are not part of the\0A *                 implementation.</li></ul>\0A *                 If the function fails due to an unsupported operation,\0A *                 the RSA context stays intact and remains usable.\0A *\0A * \5Cnote           The length parameters are ignored if the corresponding\0A *                 buffer pointers are NULL.\0A *